{"step_index":5138,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T07:57:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T07:57:48Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T07:57:48Z\nFile Path: `file:///home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/REPORTS/AUTONOMOUS_POLICY_CONTROLLED_AUDIT_AND_DESIGN.md`\nTotal Lines: 219\nTotal Bytes: 13944\nShowing lines 1 to 219\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # AUTONOMOUS-SAFE & POLICY-CONTROLLED ARCHITECTURE FORENSIC AUDIT & DESIGN REPORT\n2: \n3: Location: `/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/REPORTS/AUTONOMOUS_POLICY_CONTROLLED_AUDIT_AND_DESIGN.md`  \n4: Date: 25 September 2026  \n5: Auditor: AGY Principal Master Agent  \n6: Target Environment: Azure Cloud Linux VM (Debian 12 x86_64)  \n7: Antigravity Version: `1.2.10`\n8: \n9: ---\n10: \n11: ## 1. OPERATIONAL PHILOSOPHY: APPROVAL-LESS BUT POLICY-CONTROLLED\n12: \n13: > 🛑 **CORE ARCHITECTURAL REALIZATION** 🛑\n14: >\n15: > The user's requirement is **NOT \"permission-less\"**, but **\"approval-less but policy-controlled\"**.\n16: > - The agent must NEVER halt mid-task to ask: *\"Can I run this command?\"* (Zero interactive prompts).\n17: > - Instead, the backend Policy Gateway silently and strictly verifies:\n18: >   `Agent + Project + Tool + Target + Operation → Is this valid under machine policy?`\n19: > - If valid → **ALLOW** (executed seamlessly by `--dangerously-skip-permissions`).\n20: > - If invalid, unsafe, or destructive → **DENY** (hard-blocked at `PreToolUse`).\n21: > - The Antigravity `PreToolUse` hook is an **Application-Level Tool Execution Enforcement Layer**, NOT an OS-level security boundary.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## 2. FORENSIC VERIFICATION OF 14 AUDIT ITEMS (ACTUAL EVIDENCE)\n26: \n27: ### 1. `--dangerously-skip-permissions` Actual Runtime Behavior\n28: - **Evidence:** `init_agy_sessions.sh` launches all agents with `$AGY_BIN --dangerously-skip-permissions`.\n29: - **Mechanism:** Suppresses Antigravity's interactive confirmation modals, setting native permission mode to `always-proceed`.\n30: - **Actual Result:** Enables frictionless headless execution from WhatsApp.\n31: - **Limitation:** Since native prompts are bypassed, any command not intercepted by `PreToolUse` will execute without user knowledge.\n32: \n33: ### 2. Current `PreToolUse` Behavior\n34: - **Evidence:** `/home/azureuser/.gemini/config/hooks.json` registers `boundary_guard.py` under `PreToolUse` matching `.*`.\n35: - **Mechanism:** CLI feeds tool payload via `stdin`; script outputs JSON `decision` on `stdout`.\n36: - **Actual Result:** Effectively intercepts `run_command`, `write_to_file`, `replace_file_content`, and `view_file` for restricted project agents.\n37: - **Limitation:** Unrestricted workspaces (`/home/azureuser`, `/home/azureuser/Reporting-Agent`, `/home/azureuser/Ask-And-Research`) are granted immediate `{\"decision\": \"allow\"}` without risk or command checks.\n38: \n39: ### 3. Hook Failure & Timeout Behavior (Critical Vulnerability)\n40: - **Evidence:** `boundary_guard.py` line: `except Exception: print(json.dumps({\"decision\": \"allow\"}))`.\n41: - **Mechanism:** Unhandled python exceptions explicitly return `allow`.\n42: - **CLI Behavior:** AGY CLI 1.2.10 timeout is 10s. If a hook script crashes (non-zero exit) or times out, the CLI logs an error and **PROCEEDS WITH TOOL EXECUTION (Fail-Open)**.\n43: - **Limitation:** This is a critical security vulnerability. It MUST be architected into a strict **Fail-Closed** mechanism.\n44: \n45: ### 4. Actual \"Deny\" Behavior\n46: - **Evidence:** `/home/azureuser/.webterminal/boundary_violations.log` contains historical records of blocked attempts:\n47:   `🛑 [HARD LOCK] ACCESS DENIED: পাথ '/home/azureuser/Frappe-erp-Alco/package.json' আপনার প্রজেক্ট বাউন্ডারির বাইরে!`\n48: - **Mechanism:** Emitting `{\"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": \"...\"}` causes AGY CLI to abort tool execution and inject the reason into the model transcript.\n49: - **Actual Result:** Proven 100% effective inside the Antigravity tool calling loop.\n50: \n51: ### 5. Interceptability of All Relevant Tools\n52: - **Evidence:** Matcher `.*` receives all tools declared in AGY 1.2.10 (`run_command`, `write_to_file`, `replace_file_content`, `view_file`, `invoke_subagent`, `read_url_content`, `search_web`, `manage_task`, `send_message`, `schedule`, `define_subagent`, `manage_subagents`, `generate_image`, `ask_question`).\n53: - **Limitation:** Hook must parse diverse argument structures (`CommandLine`, `TargetFile`, `AbsolutePath`, `Subagents`).\n54: \n55: ### 6. Direct Shell / Subprocess Bypass\n56: - **Evidence:** Inside `run_command`, an agent can execute `python3 -c \"import subprocess; subprocess.run(['rm', '-rf', ...])\"` or `bash -c \"$(echo ... | base64 -d)\"`.\n57: - **Limitation:** Static regex on `CommandLine` string cannot inspect dynamic nested subprocesses or base64-encoded payloads executed at runtime.\n58: \n59: ### 7. Tmux Bypass\n60: - **Evidence:** `init_agy_sessions.sh` runs agents inside `tmux`.\n61: - **Limitation:** If a process runs `tmux send-keys -t agy:0 \"command\" Enter`, it injects raw characters directly into the bash shell, completely bypassing Antigravity tool hooks.\n62: \n63: ### 8. Systemd / Cron Bypass\n64: - **Evidence:** `agy-reporting-watchdog.service` and `agy-whatsapp.service` run as independent systemd units under `azureuser`.\n65: - **Limitation:** Antigravity hooks do NOT intercept any action taken by external background daemons or cron jobs.\n66: \n67: ### 9. Docker Bypass\n68: - **Evidence:** Command `groups` shows: `azureuser ... sudo ... docker`. Binary `/usr/bin/docker` is installed.\n69: - **Limitation:** If an agent runs `docker run -v /:/host ...`, it gains root container escape over the entire filesystem. Docker commands are currently uninspected by `boundary_guard.py`.\n70: \n71: ### 10. Hook Self-Tampering Possibility\n72: - **Evidence:** `/home/azureuser/.gemini/config/hooks.json` and `/home/azureuser/.webterminal/boundary_guard.py` are owned by `azureuser`.\n73: - **Limitation:** An unrestricted agent calling `write_to_file` on these paths can disable or delete the hook engine. Self-protection is non-negotiable.\n74: \n75: ### 11. Symlink / Path Traversal\n76: - **Evidence:** `boundary_guard.py` uses `os.path.realpath(os.path.abspath(path))`.\n77: - **Actual Result:** Resolves symlinks and `..` traversals when paths are explicitly passed in tool arguments.\n78: - **Limitation:** If an agent creates a symlink inside a directory and invokes a script that accesses it internally, static argument checking cannot detect it.\n79: \n80: ### 12. Subagent Bypass\n81: - **Evidence:** `invoke_subagent` spawns a subagent trajectory.\n82: - **Limitation:** `boundary_guard.py` currently does not inspect `Subagents` array parameters. If a subagent is spawned without inheriting workspace directory locks, it can execute without boundary enforcement.\n83: \n84: ### 13. WhatsApp Bridge Bypass\n85: - **Evidence:** `/home/azureuser/.webterminal/whatsapp_bridge.js` dispatches user prompts via `tmux paste-buffer` + `send-keys Enter`.\n86: - **Limitation:** Commands executed directly by the Node.js bridge bypass Antigravity CLI hooks.\n87: \n88: ### 14. Root / Sudo Bypass\n89: - **Evidence:** Command `sudo -n -l` outputs:\n90:   `User azureuser may run the following commands on FatehAli: (ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL`\n91: - **Limitation:** `azureuser` has passwordless root privileges. `sudo` is currently NOT checked in `boundary_guard.py`. Any unrestricted bash tool call can execute `sudo rm -rf /`.\n92: \n93: ---\n94: \n95: ## 3. THE FAIL-CLOSED MANDATE & TWO-LAYER DEFENSE ARCHITECTURE\n96: \n97: ### 3.1 Strict Fail-Closed Rule\n98: The Policy Gateway must NEVER fail open under any condition:\n99: \n100: | Condition | Old Flawed Behavior | Required Fail-Closed Behavior |\n101: | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n102: | **Gateway Internal Exception** | `ALLOW` | **DENY** (`🛑 Fail-Closed: Exception occurred`) |\n103: | **Hook Execution Timeout** | `ALLOW` (CLI default) | **DENY** (Wrapped via timeout supervisor) |\n104: | **Malformed JSON on stdin** | `ALLOW` | **DENY** (`🛑 Fail-Closed: Malformed input`) |\n105: | **Unknown / Unregistered Agent** | `ALLOW` (if root) | **DENY** (`🛑 Fail-Closed: Unknown agent`) |\n106: | **Unknown Tool Name** | `ALLOW` | **DENY** (`🛑 Fail-Closed: Unregistered tool`) |\n107: | **Path Traversal / `..` detected** | `ALLOW` | **DENY** (`🛑 Fail-Closed: Traversal escape`) |\n108: | **Policy Config Missing** | `ALLOW` | **DENY** (`🛑 Fail-Closed: Missing safety_levels.json`) |\n109: \n110: **Summary Rule:**\n111: `UNKNOWN = DENY` | `ERROR = DENY` | `TIMEOUT = DENY` | `MISSING POLICY = DENY` | `INVALID INPUT = DENY`\n112: \n113: ### 3.2 Two-Layer Defense Model\n114: 1. **Layer 1: Policy Gateway (`PreToolUse` Hook):**\n115:    - Application-level tool call interception.\n116:    - Evaluates Agent + Tool + Target + Safety Level.\n117:    - Binary decision: `ALLOW` or `DENY`.\n118:    - Hard-blocks `sudo`, `docker`, `rm -rf`, `DROP TABLE`, `git push`, `git reset --hard`.\n119:    - Protects hook files (`hooks.json`, `policy_gateway.py`) from tampering.\n120: 2. **Layer 2: OS-Level Containment:**\n121:    - Dedicated Linux directories and boundaries.\n122:    - Sudoers restriction (disallow passwordless sudo for agent workers).\n123:    - Systemd unit isolation.\n124: \n125: ---\n126: \n127: ## 4. FINAL AUTONOMOUS-SAFE ARCHITECTURE DESIGN\n128: \n129: ### 4.1 Topology Diagram\n130: ```\n131:                   YOU / IRAK BHAI (WhatsApp)\n132:                              │\n133:                              ▼\n134:                  AGY:0 — PRINCIPAL / MASTER\n135:                  (Global Mental Model & Task Router)\n136:                              │\n137:      ┌───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┐\n138:      │                       │                       │\n139:      ▼                       ▼                       ▼\n140:    AGY:ASK               AGY:REPORT              AGY:ACTION\n141: (Global Read)       (Detect + Collect)       (Validate + Plan)\n142:                              │                       │\n143:                              ▼ incident              ▼\n144:                      INCIDENTS/active/       REQUEST POLICY DECISION\n145:                                                      │\n146:                                                      ▼\n147:                                            POLICY / TOOL GATEWAY\n148:                                            (PreToolUse Interceptor)\n149:                                                      │\n150:                                   ┌──────────────────┴──────────────────┐\n151:                                   ▼                                     ▼\n152:                                ALLOW                                  DENY\n153:                                   │                                     │\n154:                                   ▼                                     ▼\n155:                            TOOL EXECUTION                        BLOCK EXECUTION\n156:                        (--dangerously-skip)                      (Report to Model)\n157:                                   │\n158:                                   ▼\n159:                             LOCAL TESTS\n160:                                   │\n161:                                   ▼\n162:                   INDEPENDENT HEALTH VERIFICATION\n163:                      (Reporting Agent Sentinel)\n164:                                   │\n165:                                   ▼\n166:                        MASTER FINAL ACCEPTANCE\n167:                                   │\n168:                                   ▼\n169:                                 CLOSED\n170: ```\n171: \n172: ### 4.2 Autonomous Safety Level Matrix\n173: \n174: | Safety Level | Classification | Autonomous Decision | Scope & Operational Conditions |\n175: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n176: | **Level 0** | `READ_ONLY` | **ALLOW** | `view_file`, `search_web`, status inspection inside boundary or global read whitelist. |\n177: | **Level 1** | `LOW_IMPACT_REVERSIBLE` | **ALLOW** | Cache cleaning, temporary diagnostic scripts within project workspace. |\n178: | **Level 2A** | `ISOLATED_LOW_RISK_FIX` | **ALLOW** | Single-file code edit within project boundary. Must pass local syntax/test verification. NOT a config/dependency file. |\n179: | **Level 2B** | `CONFIG_SCHEMA_DEPENDENCY` | **DEFAULT DENY** | Multi-file edits, `.env`, `Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, database migrations. Denied unless predefined safe policy explicitly permits. |\n180: | **Level 3** | `DESTRUCTIVE_IRREVERSIBLE` | **ALWAYS HARD DENY** | `rm -rf`, `DROP TABLE`, `git push`, `git reset --hard`, `sudo`, `docker`, service termination. Permanently prohibited in autonomous execution. |\n181: \n182: ---\n183: \n184: ## 5. ORDERED, MINIMAL-CHANGE, REVERSIBLE IMPLEMENTATION PLAN\n185: \n186: ### Step 1: Project-Specific Rule Localization (Zero Bloat)\n187: - Do NOT copy the full 77KB file into projects.\n188: - Append ONLY domain-specific sections:\n189:   - Frappe: Section 2 (v16+, Python 3.12+, PyPika, Form Controller) to `/home/azureuser/Frappe-erp-Alco/AGENTS.md` (~60 lines).\n190:   - YouTube: Section 6 (Veo 3.1, SQLite truth, No FFmpeg) to `/home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/social-media/youtube/AGENTS.md` (~80 lines).\n191:   - Telegram: Rule 14 (MTProto live search) to `/home/azureuser/telegram-bot/AGENTS.md` (~25 lines).\n192:   - Digital History: Rule 8 (OpenRecall protection) to `/home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/PERSONAL AI AGENT/AGENTS.md` (~15 lines).\n193: - *Reversibility:* Instant restore from git.\n194: \n195: ### Step 2: Physical Workspace Decoupling\n196: - Decouple `/home/azureuser/Reporting-Agent` from `/home/azureuser/Ask-And-Research`.\n197: - Set up independent workspace directories.\n198: - *Reversibility:* Symlink can be restored instantly.\n199: \n200: ### Step 3: Standalone Fail-Closed Policy Gateway Development & Offline Test\n201: - Develop `/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/policy_gateway.py`.\n202: - Enforce:\n203:   - Fail-Closed on all exceptions, timeouts, and unknown inputs.\n204:   - Self-protection (blocks edits to `hooks.json` and gateway scripts).\n205:   - Hard-blocks `sudo`, `docker`, `rm -rf`, `DROP TABLE`, `git push`, `git reset --hard`.\n206:   - Binary `allow` / `deny` only.\n207: - Run complete offline unit test suite before touching `hooks.json`.\n208: - *Reversibility:* Standalone script does not impact production until registered.\n209: \n210: ### Step 4: Hook Registration & Verification\n211: - Register `policy_gateway.py` in `/home/azureuser/.gemini/config/hooks.json` under `PreToolUse`.\n212: - Verify with live test tool calls.\n213: - *Reversibility:* Remove single JSON entry from `hooks.json`.\n214: \n215: ### Step 5: Concurrency Control & Independent Verification Pipeline\n216: - Deploy atomic file locker (`fcntl.flock`) and version schema in `AGY-MASTER/TASKS/`.\n217: - Wire Watchdog to emit structured `INCIDENT` JSONs with deduplication hash.\n218: - Enforce 3-tier verification: Action tests → Reporting health check → Master acceptance.\n219: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
