me/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/\n288: ├── AGENTS.md                  (This canonical global specification)\n289: ├── PROJECT_REGISTRY.md        (Central catalog of all agents and boundaries)\n290: ├── POLICIES/\n291: │   └── safety_levels.json     (Machine-enforced action safety policies)\n292: ├── TASKS/\n293: │   ├── queue/                 (Pending task JSONs)\n294: │   ├── active/                (Currently running tasks)\n295: │   └── completed/             (Completed tasks with evidence)\n296: ├── INCIDENTS/\n297: │   ├── active/                (Unresolved incident JSONs)\n298: │   └── resolved/              (Verified resolved incidents)\n299: ├── ACTIONS/\n300: │   ├── pending/               (Proposed action plans awaiting approval)\n301: │   ├── approved/              (Master/Human approval tokens)\n302: │   └── history/               (Executed actions and diff logs)\n303: └── REPORTS/\n304:     └── daily/                 (Daily audit summaries)\n305: ```\n306: \n307: ---\n308: \n309: ## 9. RELATIONSHIP WITH EXISTING POLICIES (OPTION C + B INTEGRATION)\n310: \n311: 1. **Foundational Directives Intact:** All universal system rules defined in [`file:///home/azureuser/AGENTS.md`](file:///home/azureuser/AGENTS.md) (Rules 1-11, 13-17: testing before applying, Bengali response language, addressing user as \"ইরাক ভাইয়া\", full file paths, no autonomous git push, mobile-first formatting, direct cloud download links) remain strictly in full force.\n312: 2. **Rule 12 Evolution:** This document canonically supersedes and refines legacy Rule 12 by replacing the combined `agy:research` model with the separated `agy:ask` (read-only research), `agy:report` (read-only audit sentinel), and `agy:action` (controlled fixer) tri-agent architecture, gated by the Policy/Tool Gateway.\n313: 3. **Project Policy Distribution:** Project-specific directives (Frappe v16, YouTube Veo 3.1, Telegram live MTProto, etc.) are cataloged in [`file:///home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/PROJECT_REGISTRY.md`](file